ed college, because, again, you stressed the importance of your family doing Family Stuff together, etc\\. I could argue it is another thing you, essentially, asked of me, but I won't, because I don't think that will get us anywhere \\(but I mention it in case it helps with understanding my side of things\\)\\. But yeah\\. I have no idea when I pushed for it, I genuinely don't think that happened, unless you mean a time we had a fight and I pushed to go anyway \\(which I think may have happened?\\)? In which case, it was for the above reasons\\. Trying to fit in, show that I make an effort to engage with your whole family \\(to them, mainly\\), etc\\.\n\nAnd then, replying I think specifically to my “I don’t know how to tell people right now”\\.\\.\\.\n\n> And I figure I'll respond to this now just for, I dunno, it just feels like I should and then circle back for the rest later\\.\n> \n> Okay, that's fine I guess? Not mentioning it, I mean\\. That isn't an \"I don't actually think it's fine\" question mark, by the way, it is just a genuine \"sure, I guess? If that's what's best for you?\" etc\\. I just\\. \\* shrug \\*\n> \n> Anyway\\. Uh\\. Yeah, I dunno\\. I don't think it's a Morker of \"if we actually do this\" though\\. Like\\. It's done\\. In a lot of ways, I think it's been done since you left after last visit\\. And that's okay, because we can go back to enjoying each other as friends\\! I think we are really good friends, I think that has always been our strong suit and I think that is why it took me so long to realize that you are a lousy partner to/for me\\. And I to/for you\\. Well, maybe mostly for\\. I do still think I put a lot more effort into trying to be a good partner\\. And I do kind of think that the fact that you seem to think it\\.\\.\\. shouldn't take effort, in a way \\(I don't mean this overall, I just mean there are a lot of things you've pinned as not worth it, a waste of time, etc\\., that I disagree with\\), is going to donk you over in the long run\\. But maybe it won't\\. You seem to be blessed with a very high luck skill\\.\n> So\\. I dunno\\. I hope you aren't foolish enough to think you've gotten rid of me as a best friend\\. Or vice verse\\. Maybe not the best friend, but you are definitely still always going to be one of my best friends, I think\\.\n> And also like I said, maybe we will pick back up at some point when I am back in New England\\. Who knows\\. I don't intent on losing touch\\- I think that was another thing that made me realize this was unavoidable, because of how I have felt about the idea of a breakup in the past vs\\. now where I don't really like it, but I'm more or less at peace with it I guess? Like\\. I'm not mad about it, I don't want to never talk to you again, etc\\. It feels more mutual than the ultimately non\\-breakup breakups of yore where you just were like \"well it is finals week and i feel stressed and anxious but i don't get stressed and anxious about finals so it must be you so i'm dumping you\" and then finals week ended and you were like \"actually, turns out i do get stressed and anxious about finals\" you know?\n> I'm rambling\\. As per\\. But\\. It's just nice to feel like I had a say this time\\. Equal footing and input and all that\\.\n> I feel like I maybe didn't finish a point I wanted to earlier\\. But\\. Yeah\\. I dunno\\. I definitely don't think it's out of the question that we pick back up in the future, that seems like a definite possibility once we have had some time for personal growth\\. Because, in a lot of ways, I think we do make a good couple? I do still solidly think that getting along as friends is incredibly important, and I think we do that very well\\. It's all the other stuff that kind of goes to cannoli\\. And even then, it isn't always bad, you know? Like\\. I am at a point where I don't feel any sort of bitterness or anything\\. I don't really feel particularly positive about the future, in a general sense and a \"people seem immediately put off by me\" sense, but whatever\\.\n> \n> I feel like I accidentally didn't say stuff I meant to just now, but again I think I need to eat/shower/change my sheets etc\\., and come back to other stuff later because I do feel a little out of it rn\\.\n\n---\n\nSo then my replies\\.\nFirst off\\.\\.\\. A thing that’s\\.\\.\\. kinda important to me\\.\nHaving once lost a friend\\.\n\n> So first off\n> I'm glad that I'm not losing a friend here\\.\n> I'm glad I'm not losing your friendship\\.\n> Because I already know how it is to lose a friendship over something, think it's necessary at the time, and come to regret it\\.\n\nThen, clarification about the questioned events\n\n> We might have gone to the movies\\. I don't know\\. Maybe not\\.\n> But we were out in the city area\\.\n> I had, a couple days prior, mentioned the Olive Garden, maybe half jokingly, because I know you don't care for it\n> And then at some point we were out and you took us to the Olive Garden and we ate there\\.\n> Had mozz sticks appetizers before our meal\\.\n> \n> I don't know anything about any trump thing\\.\n> And it's entirely possible that I am misremembering something that happened in MA\n> I just\\.\\.\\. I'm pretty confident it was two visits ago, out in whatever more urban area is nearby enough that we happened to be out there for whatever we were doing\\.\n\n> I think, I *think* that there was one time you were pushing for fireworks for Lincoln's sake\\.\n> Something like that\\.\n> And then\\.\\.\\. I don't know, it turned out he didn't want to go actually so we didn't?\n> I feel like there was something\\. Something like this\\.\n> Again\\. I could be misremembering\\.\n> I'm not as confident in this one as I am in the olive garden\\.\n\nThen\\.\\.\\. I don’t think I’m going to be donked over\\. I think I’m going to do better with a blank slate\\.\nSo in response to\n“It's going to donk you over in the long run”\n\n> I guess my takeaway is that, yes, there are things that I'm doing wrong and need to do better, and I hope and expect that I will next time around, with a fresh start\\.\n> So, I'm not\\.\\.\\. I'm not, like\\.\\.\\. what's the word I want\\.\\.\\. unconvinced? Unrepentant? Immovable?\n\nAnd\\.\\.\\. the “maybe we’ll pick up again in a few years time” attitude is one I’ve seen before from her\\.\nI don’t think she’s\\.\\.\\. actually invested in the idea, like she once was in other situations years ago where she was suggesting things like “In X years time, if we haven’t found anyone, let’s get back together”\\.\nI don’t think there’s anything like that there this time\\.\nBut I still wanted to address it\\.\nWhich is hard to do without explicitly saying, “No, I’m done with dating you because I don’t wanna”, because I don’t\\.\\.\\. there are things I’m tempted to say because it’s the end, and I shouldn’t\\.\nYou know?\nThere’s the temptation to respond to the finals week thing with “no, I’m pretty sure what I felt then is the Frodoe stuff I’ve felt a lot in the years since”\nThere’s the temptation to just come clean and be like “yeah, I’m not in love with you, I don’t think I ever have been”\nAnd I think that’s\\.\\.\\. just the wrong move\\.\nI think it’s unnecessary\\.\nSo\\.\n\n> That's\\.\\.\\. I think it's better to not entertain that kind of idea right now, right?\n> I think it's better to not have that kind of thing in the back of our minds\\.\n> I just\\.\\.\\. I dunno\\. On my end it feels like either I'm really moving forward or I'm waiting for things to come back around\\.\n> And the former is the right move, but the latter is, I dunno, potentially fed by saying \"but maybe someday\"\\.\n> I dunno\\.\n> This is probably a minor thing\\.\n\nAnd then there’s the PS4 thing, which has\\.\\.\\.\\. Flying Spaghetti Monster, this probably looks bad, but this very specific thing has been on my mind for years\nFor years I’ve been like, “If we break up, I want to do this specific thing”:\n\n> Before I forget to mention it\n> We can leave this for later, but I want to pay your mom back for the PS4 and the games she bought for it\n> She bought it for us, and then I took custody for it, and now\\.\\.\\.\n> I feel like I should just buy it off of you guys so it doesn't feel like I took it and ran\\.\n\nSo at this point, I thought I was done, and I wrote a bunch of the stuff at the top of this entry\\.\nAnd then, thinking about how much I think this situation is actually working out, I wanted to express that in some way\\.\n\n> And\\.\\.\\.\n> Thank you\n> Just in general\n\nWhich I then foolishly followed up with a variation on the above “I think I’ve accidentally lucked into the best possible outcome\\.”\nAnd I think that’s too far, that’s too flippant, and that’s probably the wrong kind of thing to say\\.\nSo we’re leaving it at “thank you”\\.\nAnd I deleted that last message\\."
